{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1467407-the-argument-for-scale-2-firearms","id":1467407,"title":"The Argument for Scale 2 Firearms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-10T20:05:07-08:00","id":1467407,"title":"The Argument for Scale 2 Firearms","content":"Having established that direct dev feedback on the topic is unobtainable (either deleted or just lost), I thought I'd discuss this as general community sentiment seems to contradict the books and I think there are good arguments on either side that could do with a little testing.<br /> <br /> OK, to start with, let's get the obvious out of the way. Regardless of what may or may not have been said in these forums by devs or others, the <b>books</b> reference firearms as being Scale 2. Pistols specifically in Core and both Pistols &amp; Rifles in Aberrant. \u00c6on doesn't give Scale for their weapons ( they do show 'slug throwers' have more tags &amp; therefore a higher <i>Enhancement</i>). Annoyingly, they don't reference Scale <i><b>at all</b></i> in their later tables listing weapons, their Enhancement, and tags. Which is what actually made us talk about it at our gaming table - knives, guns, and unarmed attacks in those tables look to have the same effectiveness and, as Aussies, that <i><b>really</b></i> struck us as being odd as gunshot wounds are 5-8x deadlier than stab wounds let alone injuries from punches/kicks.<br /> <br /> So, &quot;rules as written&quot;, guns are Scale 2. But I am a <b>big</b> proponent of &quot;rules as intended&quot;. Storypath is not really the kind of crunchy system anyone should &quot;game&quot; using poor grammar or editing. It's one of the more cooperative narrative-focused games with &quot;just enough&quot; crunch to let the yarn spinners completely run away with the story. Perhaps, being based in Pennsylvania, Onyx Path devs actually don't consciously differentiate that much between being stabbed or being shot. I will <i><b>not</b></i> rule that out having had way too many a... <i>&quot;spirited debate&quot;</i> with friends &amp; colleagues in the US on the subject of firearms. <br /> <br /> Which brings me to the difference between fists, knives, and guns <i><b>in action movies</b></i> (i.e. the oft-stated genre Trinity is trying to emulate). In the movies, at least the ones I watch, you can pound on action heroes with your fists A LOT, you can slash or stab them a couple of times, but shoot them and they are (at the very least) injured by it. John McClane (&amp; the more important villains he fights) take an absolute POUNDING in fist-fight after fist-fight. But when push comes to shove, point a gun at their chest and they either give up or die. One shot, one kill most of the time. John Wick stabs &amp; gets stabbed <b>repeatedly</b>, but gun shots either kill or severely injure. I could go on, but I think I've made the point. Whilst the movies have bullets flying everywhere, when they hit someone - they hurt. A lot. The action heroes are cool, not because they can take multiple bullets to the chest, but because they're capable of <i><b>not getting hit</b></i> (whilst taking out each bad guy with one bullet).<br /> <br /> Mechanically, Scale 2 makes more sense (for me) too because Scale with weapons isn't just about Enhancement, it's also about the Inflict Damage stunt &amp; how often it can be applied. A Scale 1 weapon vs a Scale 1 durability opponent means (at most) a Bruised and an Injury. That's <i><b>at best</b></i>, with no extra Defence from the Resilience stat roll and requiring 5 successes (1 to overcome Defence, free Inflict Damage stunt to Bruise, and 4 to Critical for the extra Inflict Damage stunt to Injure). For fists or knives, this makes some sense. But the idea that punching an action hero in the jaw and shooting them in the chest works out the same is (again, to me &amp; my table) against the tropes of the genre. Adding one level of Scale to firearms over knives/fists, makes it possible to actually Maim someone by shooting them in the chest (due to the extra Inflict Damage stunt allowed per Scale).<br /> <br /> Thoughts / opinions? (Am responding to previous comments below)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T20:17:35-08:00","id":1467409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453553-is-scale-on-weapons-set-by-tags-or-by-narrative-description?p=1467347#post1467347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regards to a pistol vs. a punch, a pistol has an advantage over a punch other than just range, and that is it being a ballistic weapon. In Core Trinity, ballistic armor is harder to come by than impact-resistant armor. Just wearing biking leathers can protect you from a punch, but it's not going to do anything against a pistol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, there is the extra +1/2 Soft Armour one can get from shopping at the local biker outlet; but we're talking about emulating a genre here. Think about Jason Bourne, John McClane, Jack Burton, Martin Riggs, even Rambo and James Bond. They're not walking around in leathers. They're as &quot;armoured&quot; as every other citizen. What makes them awesome isn't being able to take a bullet without sweating - it's not getting hit by the bullets in the first place. \ud83d\ude00<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453553-is-scale-on-weapons-set-by-tags-or-by-narrative-description?p=1467347#post1467347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to keep in mind when looking at the an example of Scale in the core book is that they were putting out a brand new system. So the examples are not always the best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I get that. It's just hard to consider they didn't intend firearms to be Scale 2 when they put that in multiple books, what errata exists doesn't correct that, and I cannot find hide nor hair of them saying otherwise in the forums or on reddit. I've personally found the fights to be a little pillow-fisted if guns are Scale 1 by default (we did try it out for a session).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453553-is-scale-on-weapons-set-by-tags-or-by-narrative-description?p=1467347#post1467347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want pistols to be more powerful than a punch but not at the Light Anti-tank Weapon level of power, then look at adding and Enhancement to it. That's how more granular differences are handled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I love Enhancement for the granular differences (say a Dirty Harry style Magnum vs standard issue Glock 22 pistol for police here). Thing is I really do think that gun shot wounds are not a &quot;granular&quot; difference from stab wounds. Statistically speaking, GSW's are 5-8x deadlier than stab wounds. In the action movies, the heroes dance back &amp; forward stabbing &amp; slashing at each other if they've got knives, but with guns - one shot to the chest or head and combat over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T20:38:44-08:00","id":1467410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453553-is-scale-on-weapons-set-by-tags-or-by-narrative-description?p=1467357#post1467357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said before, this game is supposed to be about action movies, where the hero punch can put down a target as well as a shot. The idea when a character is taken out is not about death but not being capable of combat again until get some help, so a punch can knock a person out for long enough for the fight sequence ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>For mooks &amp; minions - punching people out or shooting them, in the movies &amp; in the games, is the same thing really cos they are taken out with the one success. For main characters/antagonists - punches are generally quite a lot less damaging than gunshots. McClane &amp; Plissken can take a hell of a beating with fists, but point a gun at them and they stop. Gun are, even in the action movies, a much greater threat to the heroes &amp; villains, which is not reflected in TC if guns &amp; fists are on the same scale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453553-is-scale-on-weapons-set-by-tags-or-by-narrative-description?p=1467357#post1467357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding scale to a gun shot will make it very lethal, and giving a armor scale to compensate it will turn it into a wall against other attacks. It\u2019s not bad or wrong in any way, it can actually be interesting in a more gritty game, but the general tone of TC would not be the intention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignoring that we may or may not have the same idea of what tone the devs were going for - armor against bullets is not armor against punches. At least not without ratcheting up the expense (flak jacket vs tactical armor - more tags, higher cost). And, frankly, guns are powerful in the movies. That's kind of the point of them. We need to also consider that the players are not ordinary mooks - they have Momentum, powers, Inspiration, &amp;/or Inspired gifts to pull their ass out of the fire. To the every day inhabitant of the action hero world - yeah, a gun is scary. It should be. To the heroes who are able to utilise superhuman levels of competence (dice) for their Defence &amp; attack rolls - Scale 2 isn't quite the same threat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453553-is-scale-on-weapons-set-by-tags-or-by-narrative-description?p=1467357#post1467357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Optionally you can reduce the scale of a punch instead, and trained martial artists (anyone with 3 or more dots in Close combat, or anyone with a Martial Art edge, or what ever criteria you prefer) can attack with full scale with their fists. Or give the non-lethal tag to your fists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but that would make fist-fights even MORE pillow fisted. Drop fists to Scale 0 and the person needs AT LEAST 3 successes to even bruise your average person on the street (1 Defence + 2 for the Scale complication).<br /> <br /> Thing to note here though is that by even suggesting fists need to be a scale less powerful than <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1453553-is-scale-on-weapons-set-by-tags-or-by-narrative-description?p=1467357#post1467357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s a matter of discuss and set the tone everybody prefer in your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but my thoughts/comments are about what the DEFAULT is *meant* to be according to the rules / developers of the rules. House rules are cool, and I do use them, but it's good to know how the game is meant to be balanced before putting your hand on the scales, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T21:22:59-08:00","id":1467412,"title":"","content":"I think I exposed my opinion and more than a few options to deal with the difference between punches and bullets.<br /> <br /> Notice that a shot and a sword hit would be equally lethal in general, same for a well applied dagger in the guts. Than you must define what is higher scale and what is not.<br /> <br /> If you read the book and understand that RAW a pistol is a scale 2 weapon, I can\u2019t argue with you, not for not wanting (I would love to point references), but because there is no other point in the book to counterpoint.<br /> <br /> Anyway, feel free to follow any way you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T22:26:15-08:00","id":1467414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1467407-the-argument-for-scale-2-firearms?p=1467412#post1467412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notice that a shot and a sword hit would be equally lethal in general, same for a well applied dagger in the guts. Than you must define what is higher scale and what is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't strongly disagree here. In hand-to-hand combat, I would accept that a machete or sword is considered a Scale 2 weapon. I don't think I saw anything RAW that precludes that assessment either. Though we can perhaps infer that they considered a katana Scale 1 given it has Enhancement 3 (and Scale 2 + Enhance 3 is a bit ridiculous for a mundane hand-held weapon).<br /> <br /> As the Storyguide (or perhaps alt-rules dev), I'd provide a 2pt version of Deadly that allows for 1 extra Inflict Damage stunt on a successful attack. That could cover the lethality of a sword stroke quite nicely and perhaps allow keeping pistols at Scale 1 with Assault Rifles &amp; the like at Scale 2. Might see how that works at my table now that I've written it down. \ud83d\ude06<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1467407-the-argument-for-scale-2-firearms?p=1467412#post1467412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you read the book and understand that RAW a pistol is a scale 2 weapon, I can\u2019t argue with you, not for not wanting (I would love to point references), but because there is no other point in the book to counterpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, this feels like it's being a little passive aggressive. It's not just what &quot;I understand&quot;, it's written <b>explicitly</b> into <b>two</b> seperate TC rulebooks that way. Both the Core &amp; Aberrant books <b>explicitly</b> state guns are Scale 2 (Core in prose &amp; Aberrant in a table). I have no other reference from the devs stating otherwise. Lacking anything but the books to go on, I <b>have</b> to go by what they published to gauge their intent. If I published something twice, I'd expect the same applied to whatever it was I said too.<br /> <br /> I know we disagree on what the Scale <i>should</i> be, but please don't gaslight me on what I can see with my own eyes about the rules as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T04:52:31-08:00","id":1467428,"title":"","content":"I am not gaslighting you, I read the book and to me the scale table is wrong and going against what the book feels, but the book don\u2019t state that my opinion is right, so there is no space to me to discuss it. More than that, I think you can play the game with scale 2 guns with no issues, I understand your point of view and stated it more than once, I even explained the impacts of this decisions in your game and why I don\u2019t like them in my game.<br /> <br /> You have good arguments, I just gave up on this discussion sometime ago. I came here just to tell the advantages of both ways and the impact in choosing one option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T05:40:42-08:00","id":1467434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1467407-the-argument-for-scale-2-firearms?p=1467409#post1467409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, there is the extra +1/2 Soft Armour one can get from shopping at the local biker outlet; but we're talking about emulating a genre here.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if guns are Scale 2, are you really getting useful armor from biker leathers? Aeon gives kevlar armor (from a hundred years in the future) Durability Scale 2, but I don't think there is anything anywhere else that indicates Scale for worn armor.<br /> <br /> You also have to consider that, if worn armor is Scale 2, any armor with the Complete tag basically makes punches ineffective, for reasons you noted above.<br /> <br /> Thematically, player characters are the focus of the game, and the rules are designed to make sure random enemies don't one-shot them, and making all guns Scale 2 runs counter to that design choice. I'd make it so that things like sniper rifles, elephant guns, and guns filled with specialized (and possibly very illegal) ammo are Scale 2, but your standard sidearm is Scale 1.<br /> <br /> This also makes sense from a physics perspective; a big concern with firearms is over penetration. You want the bullet to hit the target and then lodge inside them, so some kid three blocks away doesn't get hit. If Guns are Scale 2 and people aren't, it seems like the bullet should hit them and keep going. Sniper rifles and elephant guns are specialized weapons used in specialized circumstances, and the users are presumed to be experts trained to take the issue into account.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T07:25:33-08:00","id":1467442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1467407-the-argument-for-scale-2-firearms?p=1467409#post1467409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, there is the extra +1/2 Soft Armour one can get from shopping at the local biker outlet; but we're talking about emulating a genre here. Think about Jason Bourne, John McClane, Jack Burton, Martin Riggs, even Rambo and James Bond. They're not walking around in leathers. They're as &quot;armoured&quot; as every other citizen. What makes them awesome isn't being able to take a bullet without sweating - it's not getting hit by the bullets in the first place. \ud83d\ude00</div> </div> </div> </div>Not getting hit would fall under Defense. You're also referencing people who would be Talents in the game and would have Gifts to draw upon as well as edges like Tough Cookie and the 3rd level of Precise Martial Arts. They have other means of increasing both their Defense and Soft Armor without actually wearing armor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, I get that. It's just hard to consider they didn't intend firearms to be Scale 2 when they put that in multiple books, what errata exists doesn't correct that, and I cannot find hide nor hair of them saying otherwise in the forums or on reddit. I've personally found the fights to be a little pillow-fisted if guns are Scale 1 by default (we did try it out for a session). </div> </div> </div>I would say the fact they never mention guns being higher scale in the weapons section without adding the Heavy Weapon tag a pretty good sign they don't intend them to have scale unless stated. However, this wouldn't be the first time the books contradicted themselves, especially with regard to Scale. That said, your game isn't going to break if you set all guns to Scale 2. If you like the way the game feels with things set that way, go for it. It makes things too lethal for my tastes, but if you like the way it feels, you're not playing the game wrong or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T13:23:41-08:00","id":1467471,"title":"","content":"The default assumption of the system is that the Scale of guns and armor is appropriate to the Size Scale of the weapon. (Not taking into account any tags.) Humans are Size 1 therefore human-Scale guns and armor are Scale 1. A gun suitable for a car is Scale 2, one for a Jet Fighter Scale 4 etc.<br /> <br /> However, all Scale is relative as defined by the needs of the narrative, and genre emulation comes into this. For action hero genre where the only people who die with one shot are mooks, guns and armor stay at Scale 1 - at most they\u2019ll wound a hero with two Injury Conditions but they won\u2019t kill them. For slightly grittier games, guns and armor can be Scale 2 - getting shot may kill you, and you need armor to defend against it. (If you increase the base Scale of a human-Sized gun, you probably need to increase the Scale of vehicle-mounted guns to match.)<br /> <br /> The key message as applies to TC isn\u2019t \u2018what\u2019s the absolute Scale value does X have\u2019, it\u2019s \u2018what\u2019s the relative difference between X and Y for my game\u2019.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T18:24:59-08:00","id":1467505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1467407-the-argument-for-scale-2-firearms?p=1467434#post1467434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if guns are Scale 2, are you really getting useful armor from biker leathers? Aeon gives kevlar armor (from a hundred years in the future) Durability Scale 2, but I don't think there is anything anywhere else that indicates Scale for worn armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, biker leathers are not armour against guns - they're <i>impact-resistant</i> which means they don't protect against <i>ballistic</i> armor. That said, you are making a good point about Durability scale of the flak jacket / kevlar armours. Something worth noting is that guns are not automatically Scale 2 in Aeon either, so another of those things we sort of have to &quot;infer&quot; I guess.<br /> <br /> It is a good point though. Bullet-proof armour needs to be at least the same scale as what-ever is throwing the bullets. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1467407-the-argument-for-scale-2-firearms?p=1467434#post1467434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also have to consider that, if worn armor is Scale 2, any armor with the Complete tag basically makes punches ineffective, for reasons you noted above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not ineffective - merely far more difficult. Which, to be fair, is not something that strikes me as odd. Making bullet-proof armor cover most of your entire body instead of just the torso (to make it &quot;complete&quot; against slashing &amp; impact attacks) would make the average punch/kick far less effective.<br /> <br /> That said, as I said above, the Durability Scale of armour is an important factor here. I will think on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1467407-the-argument-for-scale-2-firearms?p=1467434#post1467434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thematically, player characters are the focus of the game, and the rules are designed to make sure random enemies don't one-shot them</div> </div> </div> </div>Even assuming no extra Defence from Resilience roll, no armour, and no extra benefits at all from Momentum, Inspiration, Gifts, or Powers (what make the player characters that &quot;something more&quot; than extras in the world) - Scale 2 cannot one-shot a player character. It can, at the very best, Maim them. Also, as the successes for that attack are allocated by the Storyguide, there is no reason they need to use all of the successes from that amazing roll to Inflict Damage. A good SG might Bruise then Injure the PC, then throw the extra four successes they'd otherwise use on a Critical stunt on creating complications or pinning down the PC instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1467407-the-argument-for-scale-2-firearms?p=1467434#post1467434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This also makes sense from a physics perspective; a big concern with firearms is over penetration.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a physics perspective, having seen gun-shot wounds from a pistol, massive damage (i.e. Power/Intensity Scale) doesn't just come from being able to pass through someone. One shot to the torso can kill, without the bullet coming out the other side. I get what you're saying, but physically speaking, guns are very deadly. Even just the pistols with standard ammo. That's why we invented and use them. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T19:36:52-08:00","id":1467511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1467407-the-argument-for-scale-2-firearms?p=1467442#post1467442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're also referencing people who would be Talents in the game... They have other means of increasing both their Defense and Soft Armor without actually wearing armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, which is why <i>even a Scale 2 gun</i> would not be a one-shot insta-kill for the hero. They can use their enhanced Defence, in-world Gifts, and meta-game Momentum, to outright avoid being shot in the first place (which negates even worrying about the +2 Enhancement from Scale). However, when someone <i><b>does</b></i> get hit with a Scale 2 gun, it hurts them more than someone throwing a punch would - which makes ludological &amp; narrative sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T20:24:25-08:00","id":1467517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1467407-the-argument-for-scale-2-firearms?p=1467471#post1467471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The default assumption of the system is that the Scale of guns and armor is appropriate to the Size Scale of the weapon. (Not taking into account any tags.) Humans are Size 1 therefore human-Scale guns and armor are Scale 1. A gun suitable for a car is Scale 2, one for a Jet Fighter Scale 4 etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Always good to know the intent of the designers for this. I very much appreciate that you guys do pop in to talk to us about these things, even if it is sometimes missed in the &quot;Ask a Dev&quot; thread. I'll respond to the guy that asked the same thing in the dev thread with your answer above. Been a couple of months, but I think an answer late is better than an answer never! \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> Explicit tip of the hat to both Mateus &amp; Florin who mentioned this intent - you were right and it's worth explicitly acknowledging that. \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1467407-the-argument-for-scale-2-firearms?p=1467471#post1467471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(If you increase the base Scale of a human-Sized gun, you probably need to increase the Scale of vehicle-mounted guns to match.)</div> </div> </div> </div>As I have been following the table of &quot;Scale Examples&quot; in Aberrant, that is already the case. &quot;Anti-personnel gun&quot; is the Power example for Scale 3 (and sounds the right description for a vehicle mounted gun to me).<br /> <br /> Which does lead me to ask - why do the scale examples (in both Core &amp; Aberrant) say one thing (consistently) that is expressly not the game design's intent? Not judging or looking to judge. I'm curious because, if it wasn't for these forums, I would (&amp; did) feel justified in the conclusion those examples were expressing TC Dev intent on the topic. Especially as the examples are in two different books (i.e. across the time / writing / playtesting of two different Kickstarters).<br /> <br /> Is this something that changed after Aberrant, or perhaps during Aberrant editing but after Core?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}